.TH CREAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
creat \- create or truncate a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fcntl.h>
.B int creat(const char* path, mode_t mode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens path for writing, creating it if needed and truncating an existing file.
Creation permissions are modified by the process umask.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a file descriptor, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR umask (3crunch),
.BR creat (2)
